{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794755475,"nonce":"zbTpMbz+dCI5hmUC+/eNFpjzbso=","message":"Landed locally in d135320b7552bf8c1c70e958ac285b1f32d5c607 (not pushed).\n\nWhat is carried: a transition of transform (translate, uniform scale, turn), and of opacity on a node that fades without a group, when the transition changes nothing else. The node is painted at the pose its rules end on, which its props keep while the transition plays; the binding carries the change from that pose (the end pose's inverse composed with the current one, as a translation, a uniform scale and a turn, and opacity as a ratio). A node with a transform of its own at either end is carried too.\n\nTwo things the change needed that the issue did not list. Rows pivot on the centre recorded at paint, which was taken after the node's own transform; the painter applies a binding's scale and turn before it, so the two disagreed for a node with both (translate plus scale from a non-identity pose was 3,000 pixels off). The centre is now taken before the node's own transform, which changes nothing for a node without one. And `props.transform` of a carried node is the end pose, so a reader of the pose on screen needs `RenderTree::painted_transform`; the cn caret and switch tests read the props and now read that.\n\nHeld to the full paint (animation_paths, all three paths, nextest): transform only, from a pose, and opacity of one primitive, 0 differing pixels at 2 levels, 17 of 20 frames on rows (the first paints, the last writes the final values, one is a cache blit). A labelled card is within what glyph edges allow, as for keyframes.\n\nCost (what_a_css_transition_frame_costs, headless, median ms a frame, which includes the render and read-back every path pays): 20 to 140 cards on rows went from 3.0 to 3.7 ms with 35 of 37 frames painted in full to 1.8 to 2.2 ms with 1 of 37. The baked path is unchanged.\n\nReach: the cn transform-only transitions are the chevrons (select, accordion, collapsible, sidebar), the switch thumb and the radio dot. Most hover transitions change a colour and stay as they were.\n\nSuites: blinc_layout, blinc_recorder, blinc_app, blinc_animation under nextest, 1699 of 1701 pass; the two failures (stateful::tests::test_toggle_states and test_state_transition_with_enum) fail on a clean HEAD. One machine-local golden (cn_radio_click_midway, 24 edge pixels of the scaling dot) was re-blessed. Not run: a window, iOS, Android, web.","files":null}]}